<title>FRANCE: German rye export tender to cover 209,667 tonnes.</title>
<headline>German rye export tender to cover 209,667 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union has allocated 209,667 tonnes for a planned tender to export German intervention rye, a member country official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The quantity was pencilled into an agenda for Thursday's weekly grain talks in Brussels. But the tender failed to open in time for Thursday's first auction of the season because the regulation has not yet been formally published.</p>
<p>EU officials had said they planned soon to open around 200,000 tonnes of German intervention rye for export.</p>
<p>An official at erman intervention office BLE said on Thursday the tender was now expected to open at the next cereals management committee meeting on July 31.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
